<task id="041" project="field-mapping-server-write-path-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>FR-40: the search index follows the content type, never the user (#2502, DI-012)</title>
    <phase>2 W2 Unified RecordCreationService (follow-up; runs before W3)</phase>
    <gate>019 complete; 039 complete; owner approval of this task (requested 2026-11-02)</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Modifies .cs in Sprk.Bff.Api across RAG indexing, the create pipeline and Repair; tags include bff-api; removes DTO fields and deletes tests (deletion, TEST-MODIFYING override).</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Cross-cutting change over ~20 existing files and 8 hot-path producers (RagEndpoints, Compose, Communication, ExternalAccess) next to the per-caller retrieval trim (auth-adjacent): task-create 3.5.5b "3+ consumers, high blast radius". The design (§14) is complete, so effort stays high. Design §14.11 proposed sonnet/high; raised for the blast radius.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Edits RecordCreationService.cs and RecordCreationService.Repair.cs, which 042b also edits, and hot-path BFF files; W2 core files are sequential.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>019, 039</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, ai, azure-search, testing, deletion</tags>
    <estimated-effort>8-12 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Implement design.md §14 (#2502) exactly: the server picks the search index from the content type. Remove the index field from the indexing request types, delete `SearchIndexNameResolver.ResolveAsync` and every caller, make step 8 of `RecordCreationService` a recorded no-op, stop Repair filling the index, keep task 039's client drop, and make every stamp equal the index written. Do the read-only dev count first; leave old chunks where they are.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer, .NET 10 BFF, Azure AI Search indexing pipeline and the Dataverse write path. Follow ADRs strictly; never move a retrieval trim call.</role>
  <goal>No request field, record column or business-unit column decides where an SPE document is indexed; every index-file, SendToIndex, RAG job, bulk job and Office worker write goes to `KnowledgeIndexName` and stamps that name; no server path writes `sprk_ai_search_index` / `sprk_searchindexname` on the six search-indexed tables; search-time selection and the retrieval trim are unchanged.</goal>

  <context>
