  <steps mode="prescriptive">
    <step order="0">Branch (constraint 1); declare FULL rigor; rebase on master; /conflict-check for the hot-path files in §14.4 rows 3 and 6.</step>
    <step order="1">Read-only dev count (Dataverse MCP read_query only; no write): (a) sprk_document rows with sprk_searchindexname set and not 'spaarke-files-index', with a count per name; (b) for each of the six tables, rows whose _sprk_ai_search_index_value is set and is not the spaarke-files-index catalog row; (c) business units with an index. Record queries, timestamp and results in notes/task-041-notes.md. Nothing is cleaned.</step>
    <step order="2">Write must-fire 1-7 (§14.7) and the search-route allow-list test (AC10) failing first.</step>
    <step order="3">Make §14.4 rows 1-10 and the test updates/deletions in §14.7.</step>
    <step order="4">Drop-log level, script, docs (§14.4 row 11), and the §15.5 bullet (AC13, AC14, AC16).</step>
    <step order="5">Build; run the filtered suites named in AC12 and ArchTests (never the unfiltered Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests); publish delta; CVE check.</step>
    <step order="6">Send the diff to UAC-r2 for the scoped check (AC17); fix every finding; record the verdict line.</step>
    <step order="7">After merge: close #2206, #2413 and #2502 with the PR link, and DI-012 in notes/defer-issues.md (AC15). Update TASK-INDEX to `✅ [done]`.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the step-1 count shows any sprk_document stamp naming an index other than spaarke-files-index and spaarke-discovery-index, record it and continue (owner: leave them); if it shows a business unit whose index is NOT spaarke-files-index, STOP and escalate (the "no behaviour change" premise of §14.6 is false).</trigger>
    <trigger>If removing a resolver call would move, remove or reorder a retrieval trim call, STOP and escalate to UAC-r2.</trigger>
    <trigger>If a DTO named in §14.4 row 1 sets JsonUnmappedMemberHandling.Disallow (or an equivalent strict binder), STOP and escalate: old clients would get 400.</trigger>
  </escalation>

