  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">AC1 (step 1): the read-only dev count (a)-(c) is recorded in notes/task-041-notes.md with its queries and timestamp, before any src change is committed; no Dataverse write was made and no chunk was cleaned.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">AC2: index-file with a `searchIndexName` that is allow-listed (e.g. "spaarke-invoices-index"), not allow-listed, or absent writes to KnowledgeIndexName (RagService receives no index) and stamps the same name; a non-allow-listed body value returns 200, never 400 INDEX_NOT_ALLOWED.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">AC3: SendToIndex, RagIndexingJobHandler, BulkRagIndexingJobHandler and IndexingWorkerHostedService, for a document whose lookup, text column, parent or BU names another index, issue no Dataverse read of sprk_ai_search_index / sprk_searchindexname on any record or BU, and write and stamp KnowledgeIndexName. Their INDEX_NOT_ALLOWED retry branches are gone.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">AC4: FileIndexRequest, ContentIndexRequest, RagIndexingJobPayload and PostUploadIndexingRequest have no index field; `grep -n "ResolveAsync" src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/SearchIndexNameResolver.cs` returns nothing; GetDefaultIndexName() and its two tests remain.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">AC5: a unified create on each of the six search-indexed tables, with an owning BU that has an index, sends neither column; the step-8 trace is NoOp; no businessunit retrieve is issued for the index. Step numbers 9-12 are unchanged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">AC6: Repair writes neither column on any row; RepairSearchIndexAsync and its three reason codes are deleted; Repair's mapping still cannot write the columns.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">AC7: the OBO enqueuer stamps KnowledgeIndexName when AnalysisOptions.SharedIndexName differs from it.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">AC8 (negative): no create, update or Repair body contains either column as null; existing values are unchanged on read-back in the seam tests.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">AC9 (negative): the 039 drop tests, SearchIndexGenericUpdatePathTests, SecureChildOwnershipAiToolTests.SearchIndex*, Spaarke.ArchTests/SearchIndexDropGuardTests, the index-file authorization contract tests (tenant 403, row 409, knowledge-source 400), SearchIndexNameEndpointContractTests, RagEndpointsTests search-selection tests, RelocatedFileIndexingTests and the session-files / discovery / invoice routing tests pass with no edit to their assertions.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">AC10 (negative, UAC-r2): a test at a KEEP path shows a request-named index outside the allow-list is refused 400 INDEX_NOT_ALLOWED on the search routes, through the real allow-list check (not a mocked throw). Use an existing test if one does this (cite it in the notes); else add one under tests/integration/contract/Api/Ai/.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">AC11 (negative): no retrieval trim call moved, was removed or changed its arguments (diff of the files in the UAC-r2 constraint shows only routing lines); `sprk_isdefault` is not newly read or written anywhere in src.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">AC12: BFF build 0 errors; filtered suites (RecordCreation, SearchIndex*, RecordRepairMode*, RagIndexingJobHandler*, BulkRagIndexingJobHandler*, FileIndexingService*, PostUploadIndexingEnqueuer*, RagSendToIndex*, RelocatedFileIndexing*, VersionSaveAiRefresh*, Office quick-create contract, CrossSurfaceOwner, SecureChildOwnership*) and ArchTests pass; publish-size delta against a fresh master build (both sizes, file counts, zip tool) and the CVE result are recorded; no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">AC13 (UAC-r2): every `client_search_index_dropped` log site in src (grep after rebase; RecordTableRules.cs ~:773 and ~:780, plus any in RecordCreationService from #2514) logs at Information, ids only plus the name for the name column; a test or the notes show the level. Task 035 returns it to Warning.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">AC14 (provisioning): Audit-MultiContainerMultiIndex-Drift.ps1 no longer reads businessunits.sprk_searchindexname or reports index drift (the index half is removed and the container half kept), or the script is retired with the reason in the notes; the runbook reference is listed for task 062. The two Backfill-MultiContainerMultiIndex-*.ps1 scripts, which also write sprk_searchindexname, are inventoried in the notes and filed per /project-defer-issue-tracking if they can write a value that differs from the written index; they are not changed here.</criterion>
